\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. A rise, my soul, arise,
\par Shake off thy guilty fears;
\par The bleeding Sacrifice
\par In my behalf appears:
\par Before the throne my Surety stands;
\par My name is written on His hands.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He ever lives above,
\par For me to intercede,
\par His all redeeming love,
\par His precious blood, to plead;
\par His blood atoned for all our race,
\par And sprinkles now the throne of grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Five bleeding wounds He bears,
\par Received on Calvary;
\par They pour effectual prayers,
\par They strongly speak for me:
\par Frogive him, O forgive! they cry,
\par Nor let that ransomed sinner die!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 4. The Father hears Him pray,
\par His dear Anointed One;
\par He cannot turn away
\par The presence of His Son:
\par His Spirit answers to the blood,
\par And tells me I am born of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. My God is reconciled,
\par His pardoning voice I hear;
\par He owns me for His child,
\par I can no longer fear;
\par With confidence I now draw nigh,
\par And Father, Abba, Father! cry.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

